The Unordered West African–American Future (UWAF)
Combinatory logic, friendship, and taking turns at the lead
Flags first.
Burkina Faso is no longer in ECOWAS. It left on January 29, 2025, with Mali and Niger. This matters for the proposal in section 7.
The Houphouët-Boigny material is reported, not settled. Wikipedia's pages say he was hostile to Sankara and reportedly deeply involved in the 1987 coup. I couldn't open the Jeune Afrique piece on their relationship, so I treat this as reported.
No single naming example runs through all five countries. I use the naming events that turned up in sources: Burkina Faso's name and a street in Ouagadougou.
The ECOWAS treaty reading is from a summary view of the text. Check the Revised Treaty yourself before relying on it.
1. The examples
Sankara and Rawlings. Wikipedia's Burkina Faso–Ghana relations page says relations became strong when Sankara took power in 1983. The two leaders began discussing a union of Ghana and Burkina, with joint commissions and military exercises. Sankara's assassination in October 1987 set relations back, and Rawlings met Compaoré in Tamale in early 1988 to discuss repair. A GhanaWeb report says Ouagadougou named a major road after Rawlings at the inauguration of the Sankara Mausoleum. It was Burkina Faso's second major road named for a Ghanaian leader, after Nkrumah.
The name Burkina Faso. Wikipedia says Sankara renamed Upper Volta on August 4, 1984, and that the name means "the land of upright people."
Houphouët-Boigny and Sankara. The same page calls Houphouët-Boigny "particularly hostile" to Sankara. Wikipedia's Chantal Compaoré page says Houphouët-Boigny likely arranged Compaoré's 1985 marriage to Chantal to gain an ally inside Burkina's government, and that he was reportedly deeply involved in the 1987 coup.
Carter and Obasanjo. Premium Times says Carter wrote to Obasanjo six days into his presidency and they corresponded almost monthly. Obasanjo visited Washington in October 1977, and Carter made a reciprocal state visit to Nigeria from March 31 to April 3, 1978. It was the first by a US president to sub-Saharan Africa. They disagreed on Zaire in 1978 and on some Middle East diplomacy.
ECOWAS. Wikipedia gives its founding as the Treaty of Lagos on May 28, 1975, revised in Cotonou on July 24, 1993. It lists twelve current members, with Guinea-Bissau suspended. Leiden University reports that the three Sahel states left on January 29, 2025, citing sanctions after their coups, and that ECOWAS set a transition period to July 29, 2025 to let them reconsider. These sources date from early 2025, so check current membership.
2. Setup
I x = x (identity)
C f x y = f y x (flip)
Θ f = f (Θ f) (fixed-point combinator)
In X Y, the function X leads and the argument Y is consumed. A patron–client tie has that shape. Friendship is a term where each party is the function in turn.
3. Two models
Model A: alternation. Let F = Θ C, so F = C F:
F X Y → C F X Y → F Y X → C F Y X → F X Y → …
Symmetry: F X Y =β F Y X.
Period 2: two flips restore the original order.
Never settles: Θ C has no head normal form (it is unsolvable). The Future has no final value and exists only as the alternation.
Model B: superposition. Let Σ f x y = f x y ⊕ f y x. Both orderings are live at once.
4. Not a set, a category, or a type
Not a set: it has no members, only the equation F = C F.
Not a type: Θ C has no simple type. Recursive types can assign one, so "not a Type" is a deliberate stipulation and not a theorem.
Not a category: terms can live inside a Scott-style reflexive object, but the Future is a pattern of reduction and not an object or arrow.
5. Friendship and taking turns
Aristotle (Nicomachean Ethics, VIII–IX) separates friendships of utility, pleasure, and virtue. He also discusses concord among cities (IX.6), which is the nearest ancient analogue of friendship between states.
Cicero (Laelius de Amicitia): friendship requires equality of regard even when power is unequal.
Montaigne ("Of Friendship"): the bond is explained by "because it was he, because it was I," not by rank.
Conversation analysis (Sacks, Schegloff and Jefferson, 1974): the floor is passed back and forth.
The thesis: friendship between states is a friendship of utility when the lead is fixed and approaches friendship of equals when the lead alternates.
