7. A proposal: the United States and ECOWAS
I'm not endorsing this. It's the best case its supporters could make.
The obstacle. The Revised Treaty defines the "Region" as West Africa as set by an OAU resolution. The version I read has no admission procedures and no associate or observer categories. Morocco applied in 2017 and stalled over trade concerns. Mauritania, after leaving in 2000, signed an associate-membership agreement in 2017. Full US membership would therefore need a treaty amendment by ECOWAS members, and would collide with US trade and immigration law, which ECOWAS's free movement and common tariff would touch.
The proposal, in three steps:
An association agreement modeled on Mauritania's. The US would join as an associate partner, not a full member, with a defined trade, security, and elections-cooperation agenda.
An alternating-lead protocol. A Joint Commission would be co-chaired by ECOWAS and the US, with the chair alternating each year and meetings alternating between Abuja and Washington, as Carter and Obasanjo's visits did.
A no-consumption clause. Decisions would be by consensus, and no party's aid or security cooperation would be conditional on allegiance. This is the lesson of the Houphouët-Boigny–Compaoré pattern.
Burkina Faso. Because it left ECOWAS, the proposal should include an open channel to the Alliance of Sahel States, so engagement doesn't force a choice.
Opposing views:
Members may refuse. ECOWAS is dealing with the Sahel exit, and admitting a non-African state could deepen the sovereignty complaint that drove it.
Sankara is remembered as an anti-imperialist, so many who revere him would likely object to a US seat at the table.
US domestic politics and Congress may resist binding commitments.
Advocates of observer-only status would argue even association goes too far.
8. Limits of the analogy
States are not persons, and "friendship" is a metaphor here.
Nothing I found says these events were meant as turn-taking.
Several claims, notably Houphouët-Boigny's role in 1987, are reported by Wikipedia and not established here.
A fixed point is a mathematical object. Friendship is a lived practice.
9. Open questions
Can a typed coinductive version of the UWAF exist without breaking the stipulation?
Can alternation and superposition be unified, for example as probabilistic choice weighted toward whoever led last?
Does the model extend to a bloc of fifteen, where turn-taking becomes a cyclic group action (Z/n)?
